  "query_preview": "..Once again our synoptic pattern remains the same\nwith a strong area of high pressure dominating the Southwest. This\npattern will allow high temperatures to stay several degrees above\nnormal for this time of year, and for daily chances of\nshowers/storms. The main adjustment since yesterday was the \nextension of the Extreme Heat Warning for the lower elevations of \nthe Grand Canyon and also Marble/Glen Canyons through Friday \nevening. Although we do anticipate greater storm activity today \nand Thursday, model guidance lacks confidence on how far northward\nthese showers/storms will reach. Regardless, temperatures will be\nhot, so minimize outdoor activity during the middle of the \nafternoon and stay hydrated! \n\nThe high will push northward today and tomorrow, allowing for \nconvective activity to expand more westward from the eastern Rim \nand White Mountains. The NBM does have precipitation chances \ntapering off a little Friday and Saturday, before the high lands \nin a more favorable monsoon position for Sunday onward. \n\nIn short, expect above normal temperatures through the period, and\nisolated to scattered chances of showers/storms through the\nweekend, primarily across the higher terrain. Next week may hold\ngreater coverage for convective activity, but we'll dive more into\nthat in the days to come.",
